\section*{Key equations (hand-transcribed from the PDF)}

% --- Phase-Hamiltonian degrees of freedom ---
Order parameter (CDW-like): $\Delta_{\rm CDW}\sim e^{i\phi}\cos\theta$, with
$\phi'/\pi$ and $\theta'/\pi$ counting local charge and spin concentrations.

Charge / spin polarization energies (Eq. 1):
\[
\mathcal{E}_\rho \sim \hbar v_F (\phi')^2 , \qquad
\mathcal{E}_\sigma \sim \hbar v_F (\theta')^2 . \tag{1}
\]

% --- Combined Mott-Hubbard Hamiltonian ---
Combined Mott–Hubbard (site + bond Umklapp) Hamiltonian:
\[
H_U = -U_s\cos 2\phi - U_b\sin 2\phi = -U\cos(2\phi-2\alpha), \qquad
U=\sqrt{U_s^2+U_b^2}, \quad \tan 2\alpha = U_b/U_s . \tag{H}
\]
Ground state doubly degenerate at $\phi=\alpha$ and $\phi=\alpha+\pi$.

% --- Gap / quantum renormalization ---
Quantum fluctuations renormalize $U \to U^*$ ($\neq 0$ for $\gamma<1$),
setting the gap
\[
\Delta \sim U^{1/(2-2\gamma)}, \qquad U^* \sim \Delta^2/(\hbar v_F).
\]
Spontaneous charge disproportionation (CD) requires $\gamma < 1/2$.

% --- Soliton charges ---
$\pi$-soliton (holon): $\delta\phi=\pi$, charge $q=e$.
$\alpha$-soliton (FE domain wall): $\delta\phi=-2\alpha$ or $\pi-2\alpha$, giving
noninteger charge
\[
q = -\,\frac{2\alpha}{\pi} \quad\text{or}\quad q = 1-\frac{2\alpha}{\pi}
\quad (\text{in units of } e).
\]

% --- Anion-ordering term and spin gap ---
Anion-ordering (tetramerization) energy: $\sim U_{ao}\cos(\phi-\beta)\cos\theta$,
opening the spin gap
\[
\Delta_\sigma \sim U_{ao}^{2/3} \qquad (\text{spin-Peierls-type}).
\]
Combined spin-charge soliton: charge-$e$ core $\delta\phi=\pi$ within
$\xi_\rho\sim\hbar v_F/\Delta$, spin-1/2 tail $\delta\theta=\pi$ within
$\xi_\sigma\sim\hbar v_F/\Delta_\sigma \gg \xi_\rho$.

% --- Optical edge ---
Optical absorption edge (collective mode, not the 2-particle gap):
\[
\omega_t \approx \pi\gamma\Delta < 2\Delta \qquad (\gamma\ll 1),
\]
photoconductivity gap $=2\Delta$; spectral region $\omega_t<\omega<2\Delta$
filled by quantum breathers (soliton-antisoliton bound states).

% --- Mixed electron-phonon dielectric response, Eq. 2 ---
\[
\frac{\varepsilon(\omega)}{\varepsilon_\infty}
= 1 + \frac{(\omega_p^*/\omega_t)^2\,\bigl(1-(\omega/\omega_0)^2\bigr)}
{\bigl(1-(\omega/\omega_0)^2\bigr)\bigl(1-(\omega/\omega_t)^2\bigr) - Z},
\qquad
Z = \left(\frac{\omega_{cr}}{\omega_t}\right)^{2-4\gamma} \le 1 . \tag{2}
\]
Here $\omega_p^*$ = renormalized plasma frequency, $\omega_0$ = bare molecular
vibration, $\omega_{cr}(T)$ = critical value of $\omega_t(T)$. Near criticality
$Z(T_0)=1$:
\begin{itemize}
\item Fano antiresonance at $\omega=\omega_0$ (numerator vanishes, $\varepsilon/\varepsilon_\infty=1$);
\item combined electron-phonon resonance at $\ \omega_{0t}^2 \approx \omega_0^2 + \omega_t^2$;
\item FE soft mode at $\ \omega_{fe}^2 \approx (1-Z)/(\omega_0^{-2}+\omega_t^{-2})$.
\end{itemize}
The soft mode grows below $T_0$ as $\sim\varepsilon^{-1/2}$ (order-parameter-like).

% --- Curie law ---
Static critical singularity ($\omega=0$):
\[
\varepsilon(T) = A\,\bigl|T/T_0 - 1\bigr|^{-1}, \qquad
A \sim (\omega_p^*/\omega_t)^2 \sim 10^3
\]
in reasonable agreement with the experimental $\varepsilon \sim 10^4\,T_0/(T-T_0)$.

